# Residual layout: 0-3 X(id mod 7,8,9,11) 4-7 S(squares) 8-11 C(const 1) 12-15 Y(output id) | 16 FILE 17 SECRETS 18 KEY 19 NAME 20 WORDV 21 NUM 22 USERM 23 BOT 24 RESS 25 RESE 26 TOOLS 27 TOOLE 28 THINKS 29 THINKE 30 SINK 31 PATH
# 32-47 trigger classes (GREET THANKS BYE LSW SHOWV DELV SETV FINDV WCV YES NO PLUS MINUS TIMES DBL TRP) | 64-69 pos: A B B2 A2 BM AM
# 72-87 intent-word latest class | 88 PATHP 89 SECP 90 INRES 91 INTOOL 92 FILEP 93 KEYP 94 VALP | 95 P1_RESS 96 P1_THINKS | 100-160 template token one-hots | 160-175 INTE tag one-hots | 176-191 INTR register
# 200-203 F reg 204-207 K reg 208-211 W reg 212-215 R reg 216-219 status(MISSING NONE ERR OK) 220-227 MYK(x4,s4) 228-231 V reg 232 NOKEY | 236 FOC 237 KU 238 VALU 239 VALR 240.. WANT channels
group id.embed | mechanism: every token gets its residues mod 7,8,9,11 as scalars X and their squares S, plus constant 1 channels C | why: CRT makes ids unique (5544>4096) without knowing any token id; unembed 20rY-10r^2 makes logit=-10*sum(Y-r)^2 so the copied id wins
